<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of monthly crude oil prices spanning over five decades, identifying key price regimes, shocks, and long-term patterns.</p>
    <div class="header-meta">
      <span>January 1970 – March 2026</span>
      <span>675 Monthly Observations</span>
      <span>Nominal USD per Barrel</span>
      <span>Analyst Report</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW -->
<section id="executive-overview">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">01 / Executive Overview</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Executive Overview</h2>

    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Overall Price Range</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">${stats['min_price']:.2f} – ${stats['max_price']:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Spread of ${stats['price_range']:.2f}/bbl</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Compound Annual Growth Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">{stats['cagr']*100:.2f}%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Over {stats['cagr_years']:.1f} years (1970–2026)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Max Month-over-Month Change</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">+217.1%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Jan 1974 ($4.10 → $13.00)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Decade with Highest Avg Price</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">2010s</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Mean ${stats['decade_stats']['2010s']['mean']:.2f}/bbl</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-label">Price Volatility (Std Dev)</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">${stats['std_dev']:.2f}</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Across all 675 months</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>This report analyzes <strong>675 monthly observations</strong> of global crude oil prices from January 1970 through March 2026. Over this 56-year span, prices have ranged from a low of <strong>${stats['min_price']:.2f}/bbl</strong> in early 1970 to an all-time high of <strong>${stats['max_price']:.2f}/bbl</strong> in July 2008 — a spread of <strong>${stats['price_range']:.2f}</strong>. The compound annual growth rate of <strong>{stats['cagr']*100:.2f}%</strong> masks extreme episodic volatility: the 1973 oil embargo triggered a single-month price surge of 217%, while the 2008 financial crisis saw a $91 collapse from peak to trough in just five months.</p>
      <p>The long-term trajectory is defined by distinct regimes — the low-price stability of the early 1970s, the structural repricing following the two oil shocks, the two-decade moderation from 1986–2003, the super-spike of 2004–2008, and the elevated but volatile environment that has persisted since 2010. The 2010s recorded the highest average price of any decade at <strong>${stats['decade_stats']['2010s']['mean']:.2f}/bbl</strong>, while the 2020s have so far been characterized by the sharpest short-term volatility on record, driven by the COVID-19 demand shock and the 2022 geopolitical spike.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- LONG-TERM TREND -->
<section id="long-term-trend">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">02 / Long-Term Trajectory</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">The full time series of crude oil prices with annotated events marking structural shifts and price shocks across five decades.</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
      <h3>Monthly Crude Oil Price (USD/bbl) — January 1970 to March 2026</h3>
      <div class="chart-wrapper main-chart">
        <canvas id="mainChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>The full time series reveals a commodity that has undergone multiple structural regime changes. From <strong>1970 through mid-1973</strong>, crude oil traded in a narrow band of $1.21–$2.70/bbl, reflecting the regulated pricing environment under the "posted price" system dominated by multinational oil companies. The <strong>1973–1974 oil embargo</strong> shattered this regime, quadrupling prices overnight as OPEC asserted control over production and pricing.</p>
      <p>The <strong>second oil shock (1979–1980)</strong> pushed prices above $39/bbl — a level that would not be sustainably exceeded for another 25 years. The subsequent decline through the 1980s and 1990s reflected expanding non-OPEC supply, Saudi Arabia's 1986 decision to abandon price support, and the failure of OPEC quota discipline.</p>
      <p>The <strong>2003–2008 super-cycle</strong> represented a fundamental repricing driven by surging Chinese demand, tight spare capacity, and financial inflows into commodity markets. The July 2008 peak of <strong>$132.83/bbl</strong> marked the culmination of this cycle, followed by the fastest collapse in oil market history during the financial crisis.</p>
      <p>Since 2010, prices have oscillated in a wide band — elevated by geopolitical risk and demand growth in the early 2010s, undermined by the US shale surge from 2014, shocked by the pandemic in 2020, and driven back above $110 by the 2022 Russia-Ukraine conflict. The most recent data point (March 2026: $87.84) suggests a reversion toward the upper end of the post-2015 range.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DECADE BY DECADE -->
<section id="decade-by-decade">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label">03 / Decade-by-Decade</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Average prices, volatility, and defining characteristics of each decade from the 1970s through the 2020s.</p>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="chart-container">
        <h3>Average Price by Decade</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrapper medium-chart">
          <canvas id="decadeBarChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-container">
        <h3>Price Range & Volatility by Decade</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrapper medium-chart">
